; Five cards a segment in (pc, kind, n, pvls, pnpk), two out: cf, the filter of a stop's closure (its voice bar,
; VBAR, when the stop is voiced and the sound before it is a vowel, sonorant or nasal; else 0, silence), and af,
; the aspirated filter (ASP) a vowel or sonorant speaks its first frame through when it comes right after P T K
; (pvls) and has more than one frame; else 0. The table's cards ASP VOICED NOISE ALT VBAR come from OUT at ask.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   pc       03-31: a segment: does it need the table
  04                    INP   kind
  05                    INP   n
  06                    INP   pvls
  07                    INP   pnpk
  08                    CLA   z
  09                    STO   cf
  10                    STO   af
  11                    CLA   kind
  12                    SUB   n3
  13                    TAC   va
  14                    SUB   00
  15                    TAC   out
  16                    SUB   00
  17                    TAC   st
  18                    JMP   out
  19            va      CLA   pvls
  20                    SUB   00
  21                    TAC   out
  22                    CLA   n
  23                    SUB   n2
  24                    TAC   out
  25                    JMP   ask
  26            st      CLA   pnpk
  27                    SUB   00
  28                    TAC   out
  29                    SUB   n3
  30                    TAC   ask
  31                    JMP   out
  32            ask     OUT   pc       32-51: the table's cards, then cf or af
  33            g1      INP   asp
  34            g2      INP   voiced
  35            g3      INP   x
  36            g4      INP   x
  37            g5      INP   vbar
  38                    CLA   kind
  39                    SUB   n3
  40                    TAC   seta
  41                    CLA   voiced
  42                    SUB   00
  43                    TAC   out
  44                    CLA   vbar
  45                    STO   cf
  46                    JMP   out
  47            seta    CLA   asp
  48                    STO   af
  49            out     OUT   cf
  50                    OUT   af
  51                    JMP   rec
  60            pc      DATA  0
  61            kind    DATA  0
  62            n       DATA  0
  63            pvls    DATA  0
  64            pnpk    DATA  0
  65            cf      DATA  0
  66            af      DATA  0
  67            asp     DATA  0
  68            voiced  DATA  0
  69            vbar    DATA  0
  70            x       DATA  0
  71            z       DATA  0
  72            n2      DATA  2
  73            n3      DATA  3
